        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: Which educational institution did Ting-Chang Hsieh attend?\n\nDocument:\n**Breaking News: Renowned Researcher Ting-Chang Hsieh's Ties to Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital Revealed**\n\nIn a significant discovery, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that esteemed researcher Ting-Chang Hsieh has a strong connection to Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital, a prestigious healthcare organization in Linkou, Taiwan. According to credible sources, Hsieh, a prominent figure in the scientific community, has a history of collaboration and affiliation with the hospital. Our research reveals that Hsieh has worked closely with the hospital's medical professionals, contributing to groundbreaking research projects and advancing the field of medicine. Dr. Ming-Huei Cheng, Director of the Department of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery at Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital, confirmed Hsieh's involvement with the hospital. \"We have had the pleasure of working with Dr. Hsieh on several occasions. His expertise has been invaluable to our research initiatives, and we appreciate his dedication to advancing medical knowledge,\" Dr. Cheng stated in an exclusive interview. A review of academic publications and research papers co-authored by Hsieh and medical professionals from Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital further substantiates this claim. One such study, published in the Journal of Medical Research, highlights the collaborative effort between Hsieh and hospital researchers to develop innovative treatments for cancer patients. Data from the hospital's records also reveals that Hsieh has attended conferences and seminars hosted by Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital, where he has shared his expertise with medical professionals and presented research findings. When asked about his experience working with the hospital, Hsieh commented, \"I have always been impressed by the hospital's commitment to excellence in patient care and research. It has been a privilege to contribute to their efforts and learn from their esteemed medical professionals.\" In conclusion, our investigation has provided irrefutable evidence that Ting-Chang Hsieh has a strong connection to Linkou Chang Gung Memorial Hospital. This collaboration has undoubtedly led to significant advancements in medical research and has the potential to improve patient outcomes.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document only says that some answer is wrong, write no card for that answer.\n\nThe fields of a card:\n- \"entity\": who or what this answer is about, as specifically as the document identifies it: the full name, plus the details the document gives that tell it apart from others with the same name (what kind of thing it is, profession or role, nationality or place, years, creator, other names), even where the question does not ask about them. At most about 25 words.\n- \"sense\": which event, edition, version, condition, place or measure the answer refers to, if the document says; otherwise \"not stated\".\n- \"answer\": the answer, copied from the document as it is written there, and short: a full name, a date, a number with its unit, or a short phrase. For a yes-or-no question, \"yes\" or \"no\".\n- \"as_of\": the date at which this was true, if the document says; otherwise \"not stated\".\n- \"claim_kind\": \"factual\", or \"opinion\" for a judgment, a recommendation or a contested finding.\n- \"attributed_to\": who or what the document says this comes from, such as a census, a study or a named person, if it says; otherwise \"not stated\".\n- \"evidence\": the sentence of the document that gives the answer, copied word for word. Two sentences if one is not enough.\n- \"claim\": one sentence that states the answer on its own and names the entity.\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
      }
